{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. Multiprofile with scvi_n200 gave a large jump over singleprofile (~13 pts), aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) is essentially a wash, and image-only models are very weak (≤0.227). The one untested RNA encoder is scgpt, and we have no data on whether it could outperform scvi_n200. Question: Does scgpt, in the same multiprofile+transformer setting as config_006, beat or match scvi_n200? This is a clean single-variable comparison (only the RNA encoder changes), directly isolating encoder quality in the best-performing configuration. Why this is the best use of experiment 7: With only 3 experiments left, confirming or ruling out a better encoder before committing remaining budget to multimodal fusion or other extensions is the highest-information step. If scgpt wins, we pivot remaining experiments around it; if it loses, we lock in scvi_n200 and can spend the last 2-3 experiments testing whether multimodal fusion with the best RNA setup adds any value."
}

